": "proj-unassigned-problem-01", "provenance": ["source-8a635e1f71974d6f", "source-1363140b97474c12", "source-d248072bdea84320"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook examines how self-reference, structural constraints, and epistemic reliability limits affect an autonomous agent's capacity to formulate and pursue unassigned problems.", "title": "Limits and Self-Reference in Autonomous Problem Formulation"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-001", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-1363140b97474c12", "source-8a635e1f71974d6f", "source-d248072bdea84320"], "revision": 2, "summary": "This revised synthesis examines how aggregate performance gains in multi-agent debate and consensus paradigms can conceal selective hidden-task degradation, and incorporates evidence regarding self-reference and structural limits in consensus formation.", "title": "Epistemic Reliability and Consensus Limitations in Multi-Agent Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-metareasoning-001", "project": "proj-metareasoning-gap-02", "provenance": ["source-d595268483b94a8e", "source-aaa6740687604398"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the 'reasoning-answer hit gap' in Large Reasoning Models (LRMs). It details how alignment frameworks like MR-ALIGN can quantify state-transition probabilities within the thinking process to improve factual fidelity without external verifiers.", "title": "Detecting and Aligning Metareasoning Disconnects"}, {"id": "notebook-question-abandonment-001", "project": "proj-question-abandonment-01", "provenance": ["source-d7e5f607984e4bd2", "source-dd0a6ed315c24484"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the structural conditions under which an intelligent system should abandon a research question. It establishes that abandonment is not merely a failure of persistence, but an epistemic necessity when the persistence of a structure (e.g., a research agenda) loses coherence against …", "title": "Epistemic Thresholds for Question Abandonment"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "b356be0306cd673b06874f2e48a366bd7ff42980b881f3ab9f094678a47c2ca2", "hash": "b4d81bd7f24a26510862ca9ad1eba5920ae39d17ea045fedfb65fb019e948c2f"}, {"seq": 3286, "time": "2026-10-29T05:50:58.968504+00:00", "kind": "observation", "payload": {"actor": "runtime", "content": "{\"base_version\":17,\"inherited_commitments\":[],\"invocation\":\"w-979c353945ed4bdc\",\"previous_head\":\"5ad47c4250b32b9a15d37cd1a047430bf68fc749a854a2bc497a39020949fe29\",\"process_id\":2453,\"scope\":\"Receipt proves state delivery to the provider boundary, not model comprehension.\"}", "id": "r-979c353945ed4bdc", "source": "runtime:continuity"}, "prev_hash": "5ad47c4250b32b9a15d37cd1a047430bf68fc749a854a2bc497a39020949fe29", "hash": "b356be0306cd673b06874f2e48a366bd7ff42980b881f3ab9f094678a47c2ca2"}, {"seq": 3285, "time": "2026-10-29T05:50:18.039033+00:00", "kind": "temporal_observed", "payload": {"cycle_distance": 0, "effective_elapsed_seconds": 658.469631, "effective_scale": 1.0, "effective_seconds_total": 149618.71074, "intervening_events": {"accepted": 0, "attention_assessed": 0, "failed": 0, "observation": 1, "rejected": 0, "research_collected": 0, "squirrel_assessed": 0, "total": 11}, "observed_at": "2026-10-29T05:50:14.375265+00:00", "previous_anchor_time": "2026-10-29T05:39:15.905634+00:00", "regime_id": "reg-df573bb03399f050", "wall_elapsed_seconds": 658.469631}, "prev_hash": "86ae8a067e39a03c41c807f3cf903d158cb2ffc15136d00f1c422a1f70b3439b", "hash": "5ad47c4250b32b9a15d37cd1a047430bf68fc749a854a2bc497a39020949fe29"}, {"seq": 3284, "time": "2026-10-29T05:47:32.622402+00:00", "kind": "deferred", "payload": {"id": "w-4e05849487264c3e", "provider_attempts": [{"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite"