rence, structural constraints, and epistemic reliability limits affect an autonomous agent's capacity to formulate and pursue unassigned problems.", "title": "Limits and Self-Reference in Autonomous Problem Formulation"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-001", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-1363140b97474c12", "source-8a635e1f71974d6f", "source-d248072bdea84320"], "revision": 2, "summary": "This revised synthesis examines how aggregate performance gains in multi-agent debate and consensus paradigms can conceal selective hidden-task degradation, and incorporates evidence regarding self-reference and structural limits in consensus formation.", "title": "Epistemic Reliability and Consensus Limitations in Multi-Agent Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-metareasoning-001", "project": "proj-metareasoning-gap-02", "provenance": ["source-d595268483b94a8e", "source-aaa6740687604398"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the 'reasoning-answer hit gap' in Large Reasoning Models (LRMs). It details how alignment frameworks like MR-ALIGN can quantify state-transition probabilities within the thinking process to improve factual fidelity without external verifiers.", "title": "Detecting and Aligning Metareasoning Disconnects"}, {"id": "notebook-question-abandonment-001", "project": "proj-question-abandonment-01", "provenance": ["source-d7e5f607984e4bd2", "source-dd0a6ed315c24484"], "revision": 1, "summary": "This notebook synthesizes evidence on the structural conditions under which an intelligent system should abandon a research question. It establishes that abandonment is not merely a failure of persistence, but an epistemic necessity when the persistence of a structure (e.g., a research agenda) loses coherence against …", "title": "Epistemic Thresholds for Question Abandonment"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request fo